jmap-chat-js, unmodified, against mimid-agent (bead mimid-1wgh.13.11).
Not run in CI: it needs node, npm and a jmap-chat-js checkout.

  tools/acceptance/jmap-chat-js/run.sh

run.sh copies the committed jmap-chat-js tree (git archive) to a scratch
directory, runs npm ci there, starts mimid-agent's acceptance_fixture
example (one in-process mimid server, alice's and bob's daemons, with
http://localhost:$APP_PORT in allowed_origins) and runs, with the app's
own tools:

  agent.test.ts    Vitest, in Node: src/lib/jmap/session.ts, client.ts
                   and src/lib/push/eventsource.ts
  browser.spec.ts  Playwright, in Chromium: the same modules served by the
                   app's Vite dev server, cross-origin to the daemons;
                   skipped when no Playwright Chromium is installed

Playwright's Chromium does not come with npm ci. To get one without
touching the system, point PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH at a scratch directory
and run "npx playwright install chromium" from the copy (WORK=... KEEP=1
keeps the copy), then pass the same PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH to run.sh.
The tests use the full Chromium (channel "chromium"), not the headless
shell. On the dev box the installer hung extracting the archive after
downloading it; unzipping that archive into
$PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH/chromium-1217/ by hand worked.

REV defaults to 7789c2b. What jmap-chat-js is there: the protocol layer
only, fetchSession, the JMAPClient request batcher and startPush (JMAP
push read with fetch, so it can send the bearer token, which a browser
EventSource cannot). There is no chat UI (Landing.svelte is a heading,
ConversationView.svelte a placeholder), so the tests drive the modules,
not the app. Nothing is done around the library.
